{"answer": "{
  "summary": "Adds two-lock provenance to scripts/package_research2.py only. The software manifest is pinned to the original platform commit 481bd47fd9d62de212ed7eb4619a0554c05bc12e and the saved original lock out/two-bit-20261003/software-sources.lock.json with sha256 b9519530a4f5df872c82a4c994c496cd9667736c47668bfc26d9e09ffc0d6f0d. The FPGA manifests are pinned to the new hardware platform commit 10fd189ee705c2b14983c513c295e381fc997e2d and the current sources.lock.json. The script verifies that the two locks are identical except for the cva6 commit exactly old 6f968ec980e663046b89383b00d3dc85ce3e176f versus new a0497a8dac660f8feb19d0f486d4862777276ed3, verifies the software artifact set and hashes are unchanged, verifies hardware manifest artifacts against actual files, bundles both locks and all three manifests in delivery/provenance, and reports separate software/hardware commits and lock hashes plus the compatible-port-declaration-only note. It does not rebuild software, read build logs, compile FPGA, or claim FPGA/board validation. The board CLI hash from out/bench/idma_research remains an actual fixed-input hash only and is not associated with the software manifest.",
