    "The script still requires both FPGA manifests to have status == passed. If the two FPGA builds are still in progress, packaging will fail closed until those manifests are updated.",
    "The current hardware lock sha256 is not hardcoded because it was not supplied; instead it is pinned indirectly by requiring the hardware lock to match the sha256-pinned software lock in every field except cva6.commit, and by requiring cva6.commit == a0497a8dac660f8feb19d0f486d4862777276ed3.",
    "Changing DELIVERY.json/acceptance.json keys from the old single sources_lock/sources_lock_sha256 to separate software/hardware fields may affect consumers such as scripts/mac_research2.py; the parent should verify that consumer or provide a compatibility shim if needed.",
